A||||7||DXR_DAD||Water Pump went south.||||8||
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||05-29-2000||02:56 PM||||Well no cruzin for the Little Black Toy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I got up about 7:00am after being out of town for a few days and went to wash & wax the Toy, pulled it out to buff off the wax......and yep, green stuff all on the ground, WHAT!!!! grab the mag lite and saw a drip just under the pump (A big drip)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>And it's such a nice day today. The parts store is closed, not sure I want to spend the day fixing it. Anyway I'll ask you guys, <BR>Are there any secrets that I should know before I jump into it, and does any know off the top the price of the pump?<P>I guess I'll just eat Bar-B-Que the rest of the day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||8
Z||000001||LarryB||05-29-2000||03:22 PM||||Alan Ritter had written up a procedure on how to replace the water pump:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/waterpump.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.att.net/~fieroshadow/fierohelp/waterpump.html</A> <P>You can get remans (blah) for under $30 and new ones for around $50-$60.  Dunno if there is any practical difference between having a metal or plastic impeller. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||05-29-2000||03:35 PM||||Thanks LarrB, I just printed it, I didn't think is was a hard job, but just wanted to be sure and the printout will help, also the re-fill process.<P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000003||LarryB||05-29-2000||04:57 PM||||You're welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I came across that page by accident several months ago and bookmarked it, figuring I'll probably be in the same boat at some time. Glad to have been some small help. <P>-- Larry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||05-29-2000||05:15 PM||||DXR...When you purchase your water pump make sure you get the one with the metal impeller...much stronger.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DXR_DAD||05-29-2000||05:23 PM||||Check these prices:: Wrenchead.com<P>A1 Cardone: List: $31.10---price: $12.86<P>Ac Delco: List: $81.81---price: $40.91<P>Airtex: List: $79.94---price: $35.94<P>No discription as to the impellar??||||reg||1
Z||000006||William Federle||05-29-2000||08:24 PM||||I just replaced mine a few weeks ago (4 cyl 1984). The new water pump from Advance Auto Parts didn't have a pulley on it. It was warrantied for life. The reman'd one from Autozone had a pulley on it and was warrantied for 2 years. Both had metallic impellers. <P>I had to remove the waterpump housing from the engine and then remove the waterpump from the housing. Two hoses are connected to the water pump housing. The fitting that they are connected to on the housing has to be removed from the housing to gain access to one of the housing bolts. One of the bolts you have to get to with an extension going through a hole in the AC compressor mounting bracket.<P><BR>Going back together I used the copper colored silicone sealant on both sides of the water pump gasket, and used a 1/8 " bead of silicone sealant around the fitting that the two hoses are connected to. The gasket between the water pump housing and the engine I put no sealant on since the one that came off had no sealant.<P>Believe it or not, it didn't leak when I tried it out.<P>Good Luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||06-01-2000||08:34 PM||||Ok, Thanks all!!! It's in and all is ok!!!<BR>Got the pump from Kragen $23.00 and about two days of EASY! labor and The Little Black Toy rides again! Yesterday was to nice to spend all day under/over that car so I finished it up today<P>Now back to the wash & wax job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> . All you with black Fieros no what I mean  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
